  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (0.00) and model shows upward momentum, as market may be overreacting.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp spikes in price — especially if sentiment remains flat or negative — to avoid overcorrection.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast deviates >10% from recent 7-day average, adjust toward historical mean or trend.",
    "Increase downward bias in early forecast windows (e.g., 1–3 days ahead) when sentiment is low, as volatility often underestimates downward risk.",
    "Avoid over-optimistic forecasts when sentiment is 0.00 and recent price action shows consolidation or decline — model should lag slightly behind true trend."
  ]
